From 3a80b38c5ba1ac5c9c1d49079d5025bab67d4562 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrei-Alexandru Bleortu <me@andrei-z.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 03:13:10 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Accept FILS Request Parameters elements with only the
 mandatory fields

The FILS Request Parameters element has two mandatory fields after the
Element ID Extension, Parameter Control Bitmap and Max Channel Time
(IEEE Std 802.11-2024, 9.4.2.176), but the parser required three
octets, so it dropped the element as wpa_supplicant and other STAs send
it when no optional field is present.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Andrei-Alexandru Bleortu <me@andrei-z.com>
---
 src/common/ieee802_11_common.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/common/ieee802_11_common.c b/src/common/ieee802_11_common.c
index 0a1e9a67b..c8e1067e9 100644
--- a/src/common/ieee802_11_common.c
+++ b/src/common/ieee802_11_common.c
@@ -323,7 +323,8 @@ static int ieee802_11_parse_extension(const u8 *pos, size_t elen,
 		elems->assoc_delay_info = pos;
 		break;
 	case WLAN_EID_EXT_FILS_REQ_PARAMS:
-		if (elen < 3)
+		/* Parameter Control Bitmap and Max Channel Time fields */
+		if (elen < 2)
 			break;
 		elems->fils_req_params = pos;
 		elems->fils_req_params_len = elen;
-- 
2.47.3

